# Architecture Patterns

## Type

Desktop Avalonia app (WinExe), not a web/API backend.

## Folder map

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `Views/` | MainWindow, DocumentEditor, FileTreePanel, Preferences, find dialogs |
| `ViewModels/` | MainWindowViewModel, DocumentViewModel, Preferences, FileTree, Dock tools |
| `Services/` | FileService, Session, Settings, Recovery, LSP, AI, search, updater, etc. |
| `Editor/` | Completions, IndentStyle, InlineGhostText |
| `Models/` | AppSettings, FileSnapshot, LineEndingKind |
| `scripts/` | publish, MSIX, smoke, release (PowerShell) |
| `packaging/windows/` | AppxManifest template |
| `x-pad.Tests/` | xUnit unit tests |
| `docs/` | User/docs site content |

## MVVM rules

- Keep views thin; put state and `ICommand` / CommunityToolkit commands in ViewModels
- Own one `TextDocument` per tab (`DocumentViewModel`); editor binds to the document, not a giant string property
- Route reusable logic to Services; keep Editor helpers small and UI-agnostic where possible
- Dock shell: `DockControl` in MainWindow; documents from `Tabs` ItemsSource; `DockLayoutSanitizer` strips saved documents on load

## Feature touchpoints

- Encoding / EOL / BOM: `FileService` only
- Session restore + crash recovery: `SessionService` / `RecoveryService`
- Workspace / explorer: `WorkspaceService` + FileTree; LSP `rootUri` follows workspace folder
- Large files (>8 MB): `LargeFilePolicy` — plain open, skip folding / word completion / full-text LSP
- Keybindings: settings `KeyBindings` + catalog/applier
- Single-instance + pipe handoff: `SingleInstanceService` (Windows)

## Graceful degradation

Optional LSP and AI must fail soft. Missing servers or providers must not crash the editor.

